To force a text field to display text in columns using Adobe JavaScript, you can use the `columns` CSS property. However, JavaScript itself doesn't directly control CSS properties. You would typically set the CSS property in your stylesheet or dynamically with JavaScript. Here's how you can do it with JavaScript:

```javascript
// Assuming you have a text field with the id 'myTextField'
var textField = document.getElementById('myTextField');

// Set the columns property to the desired number of columns
textField.style.columns = '3 20px'; // 3 columns, 20px gap between columns
```

In this example, the text field will be displayed in 3 columns with a 20-pixel gap between each column. You can adjust the numbers to fit your desired column count and spacing.

